{
  "_about": "Weekly leaderboard (owner, 9 Nov). Three boards. A score only comes from an activity with a daily limit (per player, per SAST day); Supabase checks the limit in the record_activity function, so a changed client cannot post more. Rules are built from activities.csv, and from the rows of the open SunnyBay places (city.json: City job B), by src/engine/scores.js: the 'defaults' below pick the activities by what they do, 'pseudo' are the non-activity things you do (a chat, a new friend, a hangout), 'overrides' set one activity by id (board null = does not score). After a change run: npm run scores-sql  (rewrites the generated block in supabase/schema.sql; the owner re-runs that block in the Supabase SQL editor). npm run check fails if the block is stale.",
  "timezone": "Africa/Johannesburg (SAST, UTC+2, no daylight saving)",
  "resetsOn": "Monday 00:00 SAST",
  "firstBadgeWeek": "2026-11-16",
